course: dictionary
lesson: 7098
title: Peach: fruit, colour or compliment
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show you which meaning the writer means. This is context. Peach can be a fruit, a colour, or a word for something lovely, so read the clues before you decide.
explain: «The Earth is built in layers, a bit like a peach with a thin skin, thick flesh and a hard stone in the middle.» Here peach is a fruit. The sentence names its parts: skin, flesh and stone. The words a bit like tell you the writer is comparing the Earth to a peach.
explain: «The sunset turned the sky a soft peach.» Nothing in this sentence is about fruit, and the word sky points to a colour. Ask yourself: what is the sentence talking about? If it is talking about a colour, your meaning should be a colour.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word. It tells you which meaning is the right one.
fact: As a noun, «peach» means a soft, round, sweet fruit with fuzzy skin and a big stone, called the pit, inside.
fact: As a colour, «peach» means a soft pinkish-orange colour.
fact: Something lovely can be called «a peach», as in «Your drawing is a peach!»
fact: Peaches grow on trees in summer, and in «peach tree», «peach pit» and «peaches and cream», the word peach still means the fruit or its colour.
exercise: «The peach tree was full of ripe fruit in August.» What is a peach here? | A kind of tree bark | A pinkish-orange colour | *A soft, sweet fruit | A summer party
exercise: «The sunset turned the sky a soft peach.» What does peach mean here? | A lovely person | *A soft pinkish-orange colour | A kind of cake | A sweet fruit with a stone inside
exercise: Mia says, «Your drawing is a peach!» What does she mean? | Your drawing is a fruit | Your drawing is sticky | *Your drawing is really lovely | Your drawing is orange
test: What does pit mean in «peach pit»? | A hole in the ground | A kind of juice | *The big stone inside a peach | The thin skin of a fruit
test: Which sentence uses peach as a colour? | «We ate a peach by the river.» | «The peach tree grew tall in our garden.» | *«The paint on the wall was a soft peach.»
exam: In «The Earth is built in layers, a bit like a peach with a thin skin, thick flesh and a hard stone in the middle», what does the peach comparison help you picture? | The Earth growing on a tree | The colour of the rocks | How sweet the Earth tastes | *Layers, with a thin outside and a hard middle
